==Welsh==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|cy|myned||literary}}

===Etymology===
Suppletive verb; verbal noun from {{inh|cy|wlm|mynet}}, from {{inh|cy|cel-bry-pro|*moned}} (compare {{cog|kw|mones}}, {{cog|br|mont}}), verbal noun of {{inh|cy|cel-pro|*monītor}} (compare {{cog|mga|muinithir||goes around}}), from {{inh|cy|ine-pro|*menH-}} (compare {{cog|xum|menes||will come}}, {{cog|lt|mìnti||to trample, scutch}}). Indicative forms from {{der|cy|cel-pro|*ageti||to drive}} (compare {{cog|sga|aigid}}), from {{der|cy|ine-pro|*h₂eǵ-}} (compare {{cog|la|agō}}). The forms in ''el-'' are from {{der|cy|cel-pro|*ɸel-||to approach, drive}}, from {{der|cy|ine-pro|*pelh₂-}} (compare {{cog|la|pellō||strike, drive}}, {{cog|grc-epc|πίλναμαι||approach}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|cy-N|standard|colloquial}} {{IPA|cy|/mɨ̞nd/}}
** {{a|cy-N|colloquial}} {{IPA|cy|/mɨ̞n/}}
* {{a|cy-S|standard|colloquial}} {{IPA|cy|/mɪnd/}}
** {{a|cy-S|colloquial}} {{IPA|cy|/mɪn/}}

===Verb===
{{cy-verb|1s=af|irr=1}}

# to [[go]]
#: {{ux|cy|Mae hi'n '''mynd''' i Gaerdydd heno.|inline=1|t=She's '''going''' to Cardiff tonight.}}
#: {{ux|cy|'''Aeth''' hi ddoe.|inline=1|t=She '''went''' yesterday.}}
#: {{ux|cy|'''Awn''' ni edrych.|inline=1|t=We '''will go''' and look.}}
#: {{ux|cy|'''Ait''' ti i'r ysgol ar droed.|inline=1|t=You '''used to go''' to school on foot.}}
#: {{ux|cy|Mae'n angenrheidiol yr '''elwyf''' nawr.|inline=1|t=It is necessary that I '''go''' now.}}
#: {{ux|cy|Na, rwy'n '''mynd''' ar y trên bach.|t=No, I'm '''going''' on the little train.|inline=1}}

